#
# The cloudquarter build of FRR that the CQDCP gateways run: the inputs the
# scripts in this directory read. The source is this tree (the cqdcp/<series>
# branch: the upstream release plus the commits after it).
#
# FRR_UPSTREAM_TAG: the upstream release tag this branch is based on. The
#   build's changelog names it and the manifest lists the commits after it.
# FRR_UPSTREAM_VERSION: the version configure.ac carries at that tag
#   (build-debs.sh checks it). It must stay inside the series the CQDCP
#   substrates pin (SVD_FRR_SERIES): a served build outside it is refused.
# DEB_DISTRIBUTION / DEB_DISTRO_VERSION: the Ubuntu release the gateways run
#   and the packages are built on.
# DEB_REVISION_SUFFIX: appended to frr-stable's revision of the same upstream
#   version, so the build sorts above the stock package (apt never replaces
#   it) and below the next upstream revision (10.7.2 stays newer; the gateways
#   pin this exact version until the next one is qualified). Bump it when the
#   patch set changes; a published tag is never rebuilt.
FRR_UPSTREAM_TAG=frr-10.7.1
FRR_UPSTREAM_VERSION=10.7.1
DEB_DISTRIBUTION=noble
DEB_DISTRO_VERSION=24.04
DEB_REVISION_SUFFIX=+cqdcp1
